"holder":"Lettie VAN ZYL","year":1977,"type":"overall"},"womenHeroicSecond":{"name":"Sue WAGNER","time":"08:43:00","athleteId":"A5A8C038-243E-499D-A40C-373D49DBBFBC","brokenRecord":{"time":"08:58:00","holder":"Lettie VAN ZYL","year":1977,"type":"overall"}},"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1922,"mensWinner":"Arthur NEWTON","mensTime":"08:40:00"}},"narrative":"The 1978 Comrades Marathon was the 53rd running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.900 km. The race was held on Wednesday, 31 May. Conditions: Cold at start, warming to mild with short intervals of rain in places after halfway. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nAlan ROBB claimed the men's title in 05:29:14, ahead of Dave WRIGHT (05:48:00) and Anton DE KONING (05:49:00). Lettie VAN ZYL won the women's race in 08:25:00, followed by Sue WAGNER (08:43:00).\n\nAlan ROBB's 05:29:14 set a new course record, beating Dave LEVICK's 05:39:09 from 1973. Lettie VAN ZYL's 08:25:00 broke her own women's course record of 08:58:00 from 1977. Women's runner-up Sue WAGNER's 08:43:00 also beat the previous women's record. Lettie VAN ZYL's 08:25:00 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1922 (Arthur NEWTON, 08:40:00).\n\nFrom a field of 2,600 entries, 2,600 runners crossed the finish line (100.0% completion rate), with athletes representing over 10 countries. The field comprised 2,590 men and 10 women (0.4% female). The average finish time was 08:56:41.\n\nMedals awarded: 10 Gold, 394 Silver, 2,196 Bronze. 1,151 runners (44.3%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was SHIPTON in 10:59:00.\n\nCompared to the previous down run in 1976, the field was 84.7% larger.","countryDataPct":100.0}